  - L06-P2 · Inflation equals expected inflation exactly when output is potential Under A1 and A2, show that \(\pi_t = \pi^{e}_t\) if and only if \(Y_t = \bar Y\).
  - Solution Both inflation rates use the same denominator, since \(\pi_t = (P_t - P_{t-1})/P_{t-1}\) and \(\pi^{e}_t = (P^{e}_t - P_{t-1})/P_{t-1}\).
  - Hence \(\pi_t = \pi^{e}_t\) if and only if \(P_t = P^{e}_t\).
  - By A1, \(P_t = P^{e}_t\) if and only if \(Y_t - \bar Y = \nu (P_t - P^{e}_t) = 0\), which is \(Y_t = \bar Y\).
  - So every unemployment rate at which output is potential equals \(u^{n}\).
